# G071 — Address Book

*v2. See `address-book.md` for prose: canonical email/phone, duplicate detection
via canonical-form equivalence classes, merge preserves union of fields.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault People Gallery

[people-gallery @vcard-dir
    IN ORDER TO
        load vcards, surface duplicate groups for user review
        merge confirmed duplicates, and support live search

    @ab <- [contacts[load {path: @vcard-dir + "/*.vcard"}]]
    @dupes <- [contacts[find-duplicates {book: @ab}]]

    for @group in @dupes
        @names <- @group mapped to ([contacts[get {book: @ab, id: @id}]]):name
        [ui[suggest-merge {ids: @group, names: @names}]]

    sync @user-events {
        confirm-merge @ids ->
            @merged <- [contacts[merge {book: @ab, ids: @ids}]]
            [vault[save {path: "people/" + @merged + ".vcard"}]]
            for @id in @ids [fs[delete {path: "people/" + @id + ".vcard"}]]

        search @query ->
            @by-name  <- [contacts[search-by-name  {book: @ab, needle: @query}]]
            @by-email <- [contacts[search-by-email {book: @ab, email: @query}]]
            [ui[render-results {ids: @by-name ∪ @by-email}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[contacts
    canonical-email      {email}           ;; lowercase, +alias stripped
    canonical-phone      {phone}            ;; digits only, country-code normalized
    new
    add                  {book, contact}
    get                  {book, id}         ;; || not-found
    find-duplicates      {book}              ;; -> [[id]] equivalence classes
    merge                {book, ids}         ;; || merge-conflict
    search-by-name       {book, needle}
    search-by-email      {book, email}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: canonical form as `where` invariant

[contacts[find-duplicates {book: @b}
    where
        two contacts are duplicates iff they share a canonical email
        or share a canonical phone
        (canonical form is defined by canonical-email / canonical-phone)
        and the result groups contacts into equivalence classes by this relation
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @ab <- [contacts[new]]
    [contacts[add {book: @ab, contact: {name: "Alice Smith",
                                         email: "Alice+newsletter@Example.COM"}}]]
    [contacts[add {book: @ab, contact: {name: "Alice S.",
                                         email: "alice@example.com"}}]]
    [contacts[add {book: @ab, contact: {name: "Bob",
                                         email: "bob@example.com"}}]]

    -> [contacts[find-duplicates {book: @ab}]]
    ;; -> [[1, 2]]  (same canonical email)
]
